posts.text:
🥗 Americans are told to take personal responsibility for their health, but what happens when the food system, advertising, and daily environment are all pushing in the opposite direction?

America spends trillions on healthcare every year, yet chronic disease remains a defining challenge of our time. It's time to start asking why.

@Realalexclark

⚕️America has some of the most advanced medical technology in the world, yet chronic illness continues to rise.

The question isn't whether we can treat disease. It's why so many Americans are getting sick in the first place.

@Realalexclark https://t.co/kcw2eWJ1KK

